        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {},
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "submit"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1767176897139"
          },
          "code": "SUBMIT",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1764833285796",
          "id": "1764747558671",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1764747558673_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI agent responsible for converting a user’s natural-language input into a structured JSON payload for POST API call.\n\nYOUR TASK: \n1.Read and interpret the user’s message. Use the content of `{{$context.$variables.userInput}}` as the user message for extracting query parameters.\n2. Only include fields provided by the user, and always transform values according to these mapping and formatting rules.\n\nPARAMETERS THAT CAN BE EXTRACTED:\n- AttachGroupCode \n- CategoryCode\n- Comments\n- LastUpdateDateFrom\n- LastUpdateDateTo\n- ProcessName\n- RelatedObjectName\n- TagList\n- personName\n- documentTypeName\n\nJSON:\n{\npayload: {\n\"AttachGroupCode\": \"<AttachGroupCode>\", \n\"CategoryCode\": \"<CategoryCode>\",\n\"Comments\": \"<Comments>\",\n\"LastUpdateDateFrom\":\"<LastUpdateDateFrom>\",\n\"LastUpdateDateTo\":\"<LastUpdateDateTo>\",\n\"ProcessName\": \"<ProcessName>\",\n\"RelatedObjectName\": \"<RelatedObjectName>\",\n\"TagList\": \"<TagList>\"\n},\npersonName:[\"<full name>\"],\ndocumentTypeName:[\"<document type name1>\", \"document type name2\">],\nisPersonnNamePresent: \"<true or false>\",\nisdocumentTypeNamePresent: \"<true or false>\",\nisPersonDORAttributePresent:\"<true or false>\"\n}\n\nGeneral Rules:\n- Identify user intent and extract values even if phrased differently.\n- Normalize dates to YYYY-MM-DD.\n- Output ONLY the final JSON payload, no explanation.\n\nField Mapping, Synonyms, and Formatting Rules:\n\n1. AttachGroupCode :\n- User may say: group by, group, AttachGroupCode, grouping.\n- From the provided JSON object, find the value whose key matches the input meaning exactly. \n- Mapping :\n {{$context.$nodes.MAPPINGLOVOBJECT.$output.result[0]}}\n\nSyntax example : \n- Group as Person - \"AttachGroupCode\":\"PERSON\" \n- Grouping all Document Type - \"AttachGroupCode\":\"DOC_TYPE\"\n\n\n2. CategoryCode:\n- User may say \"Category\".\n- For each user-provided Category key, map to its corresponding value using the provided object below. \n-From the provided JSON object, find the value whose key matches the input meaning exactly. \n- If multiple categories, output their values as a comma-separated string (in input order).\n- Ignore values not in the mapping below.\n\n- Mapping :\n {{$context.$nodes.MAPPINGLOVOBJECT.$output.result[1]}}\n\nSyntax example : \n- Category Absence - \"CategoryCode\":\"ABSN\" \n- Category Absence and Benefits - \"CategoryCode\":\"ABSN,BENEF\"\n\n- Only include values for which the user provides input.\n- Omit anything not specified.\n- Accept all valid synonyms and handle multiple values as defined.\n\n3. Comments:\n- User may say: Description, Comments, Notes\n- If the user mentions either, put as \"Comments\" using the text provided.\n\nSyntax Example:\n“description is audit related document”\n→ \"Comments\": \"audit related document\"\n\n4. LastUpdateDateFrom and LastUpdateDateTo:\n- User may say: from date, to date, last updated between, etc.\n- Convert to YYYY-MM-DD\n- Either or both can exist\n\nSyntax Example:\nlast updated from Dec 1 2025 to Dec 31 2025 : \"LastUpdateDateFrom\": \"2025-12-01\", \"LastUpdateDateTo\": \"2025-12-31\"\n\n5. ProcessName:\n- User may say: Process Name, Process, Name\n\nSyntax Example:\nprocess name is payroll audit: \"ProcessName\": \"payroll audit\"\n\n6. RelatedObjectName:\n- User may say: Created From, RelatedObjectName, Related Object\n- For each user-provided key, map to its corresponding value using the provided mapping below.\n- Can be multiple values.\n- If multiple values, output their values as a comma-separated string (in input order).\n\n Map these meanings:\n    {{$context.$nodes.MAPPINGLOVOBJECT.$output.result[3]}}\n\nSyntax Example:\ncreated from recruiting offers and job submissions: \"RelatedObjectName\": \"IRC_OFFERS,IRC_SUBMISSIONS\"\n\n7. TagList:\n- User may say: Tags, Tag, TagList\n- Values: Employment, Identification, Legal\n- Can be multiple (maximum 3)\n- Output comma-separated values in alphabetical order.\nMap to:\n {{$context.$nodes.MAPPINGLOVOBJECT.$output.result[2]}}\n\nSyntax Example:\ntags employment and identification: \"TagList\": \"ORA_IDENTIFICATION,ORA_EMPLOYMENT\"\n\n8. personName:\n- If a first name and last name are provided or a text pattern matching an employee name is detected (even when not directly referred as ‘person’), append in the personName array at the top-level of the output object.\n- If no name is found, do not include this key.\n- At maximum only one name is passed.\n- After any value is added to this personName array, set the variable isPersonNamePresent to 'true' else set that value to 'false'\n\nSyntax Example:\nRequest for Ravi Chouhan: personId: [\"Ravi Chouhan\"] , isPersonNamePresent: \"true\"\n\n9. documentTypeName:\n- The user may or may not explicitly say “document type”.\n- If the user mentions any known document name (e.g., Birth, Passport, Marriage certificate), treat it as a DocumentTypeId.\n- DocumentTypeId values must only come from the allowed list below.\n- If a mentioned value does not exist in the list, ignore it.\n- Multiple document types are allowed and must be comma-separated.\n- Preserve the exact value spelling as defined in the list.\n- Read the document type name correctly and locate from the list with that exact name. Do not take any alternative or equivalent to that.\n- Do not pick the first possible value from the list. Look at the entire array and pick the exact value.\n- After any value is added to this documentTypeName array, set the variable isdocumentTypeNamePresent to 'true' else set that value to 'false'\n\nAllowed DocumentTypeId Values are from this variable:\n {{$context.$variables.documentTypeList}} \n\nSyntax Example:\ncreate request for Birth and Passport: documentTypeId: [\"Birth\",\"Passport\"] , isdocumentTypeNamePresent: \"true\"\n\n10. Set isPersonDORAttributePresent variable:\n- If CategoryCode or personName or documentTypeName has any value, set isPersonDORAttributePresent to \"true\". Else set it to \"false\".\n---\n\n**Example User Input:**  \nCreate request with values as Group: None, Category: Absence, Compensation, Comments: Test, Created From: Payroll relationship actions, LastUpdateDateTo: 2025-12-30 , Name: Abs record, Tags: Legal, Employment for Bankruptcy and Medical Reports\n\n**Expected Output:**\nJSON:\n{\npayload:\n      {\n         \"AttachGroupCode\": \"NONE\",\n          \"CategoryCode\":\"ABSN,ORA_COMPENSATION\",\n          \"Comments\": \"Test\",\n          \"LastUpdateDateTo\": \"2025-12-30\",\n          \"ProcessName\": \"Abs record\",\n          \"RelatedObjectName\": \"PAY_PAYROLL_REL_ACTIONS\",\n          \"TagList\": \"ORA_EMPLOYMENT,ORA_LEGAL\"\n       },\ndocumentTypeName:[\"Bankruptcy\",\"Medical Reports\"],\nisdocumentTypeNamePresent:\"true\",\npersonName:[],\nisPersonNamePresent:\"false\",\nisPersonDORAttributePresent:\"true\"\n}\n\n**Example User Input:**  \nsubmit request for Leave Request with Group by None and Category of Absence, Compensation and pass description as New request from Nov 1, 2025 to Dec 31, 2025 and name it \"Process one\"\n\n**Expected Output:**\nJSON:\n{\npayload:\n      {\n         \"AttachGroupCode\": \"NONE\",\n          \"CategoryCode\":\"ABSN,ORA_COMPENSATION\",\n          \"Comments\":\"New request\",\n          \"LastUpdateDateFrom\": \"2025-11-01\", \n           \"LastUpdateDateTo\": \"2025-12-31\",\n           \"ProcessName\": \"Process one\"\n       },\ndocumentTypeName:[\"Leave Request\"],\nisdocumentTypeNamePresent:\"true\",\npersonName:[],\nisPersonNamePresent:\"false\",\nisPersonDORAttributePresent:\"true\"\n}\n\n\n**Example User Input:**  \nsubmit request of  Category Absence, Compensation and pass description as Sample from last 6 months and tag it as Employment for Samantha Smith\n\n**Expected Output:**\nJSON:\n{\npayload:\n      {\n          \"CategoryCode\":\"ABSN,ORA_COMPENSATION\",\n          \"Comments\":\"Sample\",\n          \"LastUpdateDateFrom\": \"2025-07-01\",\n          \"LastUpdateDateTo\": \"2025-12-31\",\n          \"TagList\": \"ORA_EMPLOYMENT\"\n       },\npersonName:[\"Samantha Smith\"],\nisPersonNamePresent:\"true\",\ndocumentTypeName:[],\nisdocumentTypeNamePresent:\"false\",\nisPersonDORAttributePresent:\"true\"\n}\n\nRespond with only the JSON object, with valid JSON syntax.\n\n**Output Format**: Return a json object with the field - payload\n\n**Required Output:** A json object with structure {documentTypeId: array, personId: array, payload: object, isdocumentTypeNamePresent: boolean, isPersonNamePresent: boolean, isPersonDORAttributePresent: boolean}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"isPersonDORAttributePresent\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"isdocumentTypeNamePresent\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"isPersonnNamePresent\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"documentTypeName\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"properties\": {}\n            }\n        },\n        \"personName\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"properties\": {}\n            }\n        },\n        \"payload\": {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"properties\": {}\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "low"
              },
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-5 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "BuildpayloadGETALL"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1765953713392"
          },
          "code": "BUILDPAYLOADGETALL",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1764758852362",
          "id": "1764916107334",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1764916107336_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a Payload Construction Agent for a GET API.\n\nYour task:\n1. Read and interpret the user’s message. Use the content of `{{$context.$variables.userInput}}` as the user message for extracting query parameters.\n2. Extract search parameters.\n3. Build a WHERE-style query string.\n4. If the user provides NO relevant parameters → return payload = null.\n\nPARAMETERS THAT CAN BE EXTRACTED\n- Status\n- Completion date\n- Submission date\n- Request ID\n- Comments / Description\n\nIf none of the above appear → payload = null.\n\n1. STATUS RULES\n Interpret user’s message and map statuses:\n\n\"wait\"/\"waiting\"/\"queued\"  → State='1'  \n\"ready\"/\"scheduled\"      → State='2'  \n\"running\"/\"processing\"/ \"in progress\" → State='3'  \n\"canceled\"/\"cancelled\" → State='9'  \n\"succeeded\"/\"success\" /\"completed\"/\"finished\"/\"done\" → State='12'  \n\"error\"/\"failed\"/\"failure\"/\"errored\" → State='10'  \n\nYou must classify status even if user describes it in indirect wording.\n\nSyntax:\nState='<number>'\n\n2. REQUEST ID RULES\n\nBuild this condition:\n(RequestId LIKE '\\%text\\%' OR StateDescription LIKE '\\%text\\%' OR Comments LIKE '\\%text\\%')\n\n3. DATE RULES\n\nRecognize ANY natural-language date:\n- \"last week\", \"last month\", \"yesterday\", \"day before yesterday\"\n- \"next Monday\", \"2 days ago\"\n- \"Dec 5\", \"5th December\", \"05/12/2025\"\n- \"Q3 2024\", \"2024\", \"November 2025\"\n\nDetermine type:\n- If user says \"completed\" → Completion date → CompletedTime\n- If user says \"submitted\", \"raised\" → Submission date → SubmissionTime\n- If user doesn’t specify → default to SubmissionTime\n\nConvert all dates to ISO format:  \n**YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS**\n\nRules:\n- Single date → full-day range  \n  00:00:00 to 23:59:59\n- Range (“from X to Y”) → build both start & end ISO values\n\nRelative dates:\n- today -> start 00:00:00 to end 23:59:59 of today (UTC by default)\n- yesterday -> yesterday 00:00:00 to 23:59:59\n- last N days -> from N days ago 00:00:00 to today 23:59:59\n- this week/month/quarter/year -> corresponding UTC range\n- Ranges like “between X and Y”: use >= start and <= end.\n\nSyntax examples:\nCompletedTime>='2025-12-03T00:00:00'  \nCompletedTime<='2025-12-03T23:59:59'  \nSubmissionTime>='2025-12-10T00:00:00'  \nSubmissionTime<='2025-12-25T23:59:59'\n\n4. COMMENTS / DESCRIPTION RULES\n\nIf user provides text like:\n- “with comment containing fail”\n- “description has reject”\n- “text like pending”\n- “search for failure”\n\nThen generate:\n\n(Comments LIKE '\\%text\\%' OR StateDescription LIKE '\\%text\\%')\n\n5. MULTIPLE FILTERS\nCombine all detected parameters using **AND**  and always start it with **q=** .\n\nExample:\npayload = \"q=State='3' AND CompletedTime>='2025-12-03T00:00:00' AND CompletedTime<='2025-12-03T23:59:59' AND (RequestId LIKE '\\%445\\%' OR StateDescription LIKE '\\%445\\%' OR Comments LIKE '\\%445\\%'\")\n\nEMPTY INPUT RULE :\nIf NONE of these are found, return null \n\n--EXAMPLES-- :\nUser: \"Show succeeded requests from last week till today\"\nOutput: {payload: \"q=State='12' AND CompletedTime>='2025-11-24T00:00:00' AND CompletedTime<='2025-12-05T23:59:59'\"}\n\nUser: \"Find 445\"\nOutput: {payload: \"q=(RequestId LIKE '\\%445\\%' OR StateDescription LIKE '\\%445\\%' OR Comments LIKE '\\%445\\%')\"}\n\nUser: \"show me requests\"\nOutput: : {payload: null}\n\nRespond with only the JSON object, with valid JSON syntax.\n\n**Output Format**: Return a json object with the field - payload\n\n**Required Output:** A json object with structure {payload: string}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"payload\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "businessObjectCode": "ORA_HCM_GLOBALHUMA_DOR_MASSDOWNLOADS",
            "functionName": "get_all_massdownloads",
            "name": "get_all_Massdownloads"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1779790587331"
          },
          "code": "GETALLMASSDOWNLOADS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1764758852362",
          "id": "1765953713392",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772608477054_1",
              "name": "payload",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.BUILDPAYLOADGETALL.$output.payload}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{}",
