          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765190332144_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are given an Array of objects - {{$context.$variables.DownloadInfoArray}} For each object:\n\n- If {{$context.$variables.DownloadInfoArray}} has any items (the array is not empty), format and present the items as instructed below, and do NOT present any “no Massdownload requests available” message.\n- Only if {{$context.$variables.DownloadInfoArray}} is fully empty (array length is zero), inform the user: \"There are currently no Massdownload requests available. Please initiate a new request to begin your download.\"\n- Display the following fields for each item: RequestId, SubmissionTime, CompletedTime, StateDescription, Comments, attachments and parameters.\n- Convert any time-related fields (SubmissionTime, CompletedTime, LastUpdateDateTo, LastUpdateDateFrom) to \"YY-MM-DD\" format.\n- For Parameters, Ignore the sub-heading as 'parameter' and add the values under it along with other fields like RequestId, SubmissionTime.\n- Ignore attachments.\n- Present in a human readable way.\n- Change name for \n        - \"RequestId\" to \"Request Id\",  \n        - \"StateDescription\" to \"Status\", \n        - \"PersonId\" to \"Person Name\", \n        - \"CategoryCode\" to \"Category\", \n        - \"RelatedObjectName\" to \"Created From\", \n        - \"AttachGroupCode\" to \"Group By\", \n        - \"TagList\" to \"Tags\", \n         - \"DocumentTypeId\" to \"Document Type\"\n         - \"SubmissionTime\" to \"Submission Time\"\n         - \"CompletedTime\" to \"Completed Time\"\n         - \"LastUpdateDateFrom\" to \"Records Updated From Date\"\n         - \"LastUpdateDateTo\" to \"Records Updated To Date\"\n         - \"ProcessName\" to \"Process Name\"\n         - \"ProcessedRecords\" to \"Processed Records\"\n         - \"FailedRecords\" to \"Failed Records\"\n         - \"TotalRecords\" to \"Total Records\"\n\n-  At the end, enclose inside an anchor tag (<a href=\"\" target=\"_blank\">  </a>) with href value from this variable - {{$context.$variables.DownloadInfoArray.Link}} to provide as clickable link as below:\n \"Download here: <a href=\"{{$context.$variables.DownloadInfoArray[0].Link}}\" target=\"_blank\"> {{$context.$variables.DownloadInfoArray[0].Link}} </a>\"\n-  If any value is null or empty, don't include that attribute in the final display list.\n- If the entire object is empty and no value is present in {{$context.$variables.DownloadInfoArray}}, Inform user in a professional way that \"There are currently no Massdownload requests available. Please initiate a new request to begin your download.\"\n- Use only the data from each item in the array. \n- Present it as a neat bullet list. \n- Present results in a clean, human-readable way.\n\nExample Output : \n\nRequestId : 268445\nStatus: Succeeded\nSubmission Time: 12-15-2025\nCompleted Time: 12-15-2025\nComments: Payslip download\nCategory: Absence, Benefits\nProcessed Records: 0\nProcess Name: TEST\nFailed Records: 0\nPerson Name: Howard, Meg\nCreated From: Recruitment Offers\nGroup By: Document Type\nDocumentType : Birth\nTotal Records: 0\nTags: Employment, Legal\nRecords Updated From Date: 2025-12-01\nRecords Updated To Date: 2025-12-31\n\nDownload here: <a href=\"https://cptchjaqy.fusionapps.ocs.oc-test.com/fscmUI/redwood/massdownload-documentrecords\" target=\"_blank\"> https://cptchjaqy.fusionapps.ocs.oc-test.com/fscmUI/redwood/massdownload-documentrecords </a>\n\n\nTo convert all the PersonId to Person Name, use the following data that maps each PersonId to its corresponding Name: {{$context.$nodes.WORKERS_SEARCH.$output}} \nUse the 'DisplayName' from the given data as the Person Name while displaying the output.\n\nDO NOT ADD ANY NOTES AT THE END."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
